+	 * been whatever the heap happened to hold. H.264 has been decoding
+	 * bit-exact by luck.
+	 *
+	 * cedrus wants no start code for EITHER codec -- it advertises
+	 * V4L2_STATELESS_H264_START_CODE_NONE and
+	 * V4L2_STATELESS_HEVC_START_CODE_NONE, both as .max and .def, so NONE is
+	 * the only value it accepts. Measured both ways: prepending one makes
+	 * HEVC hand the decoder three bytes it was told not to expect (the
+	 * OUTPUT payload came out three bytes longer than GStreamer's for the
+	 * same stream, and the NAL type then read out of the start code as 0),
+	 * and it makes H.264 decode non-bit-exact.
+	 *
+	 * Hardcoding false is right for this driver and wrong in general. The
+	 * correct form is to query the per-codec START_CODE control and honour
+	 * whatever it reports, which is what the dead h264_get_controls() was
+	 * reaching for; a driver that wants ANNEX_B would need that.
+	 */
+	context_object->h264_start_code = false;
